meta {
  name: Get collection (top-up account) config
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/config/collection
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

assert {
  res.body.statusCode: isDefined
}

tests {
  test("prints each collection setting", function() {
    expect(res.body.statusCode).to.equal(200);
    const d = res.body.data || {};
    const c = d.config || d;
    Object.keys(c).forEach(k => console.log(k + ": " + JSON.stringify(c[k])));
  });
}

docs {
  The wallet top-up (collection) account settings (`CollectionSettings`, DynamicConfig namespace `collection`). Each plutus
  server re-reads them on its polling interval, so a change reaches every server without a deploy.

  The keys that decide what the app shows on `GET /api/virtual-accounts/torg/{torgId}/collection-accounts`:

  | Key | Meaning |
  |---|---|
  | `defaultProvider` | the primary account's provider, `YES_BANK` unless a torg has an override |
  | `alternateDisplay` | how the second account (Razorpay Smart Collect, Axis IFSC `UTIB`) is shown: `OFF` hidden, `HIDDEN` hidden, `COMING_SOON` without number, `AVAILABLE` in full |
  | `razorpayEnabled` | Razorpay kill switch. Don't use it just to hide the account: it also stops Razorpay settlement recon |
  | `provisionAlternateOnWalletCreate` | new torgs also get a (hidden) Razorpay account at wallet creation |

  Needs a VAHN_ADMIN token in `accessToken`. To change `alternateDisplay`, use "Set collection alternate display".
}
